=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play logs/unreadable -----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's Logs screen (pkg/screens/logs), inferred$
# from v0.3.2 and origin/main, read from a simulated host by the$
# real reader (pkg/engine/logview). It only reads: no plan, no$
# y/N, no journal. No pager runs: Open says what hardn would$
# run. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and file$
# is the fake's.$
$
# Info: logs/unreadable$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, less installed.$
# /var/log/hardn.log is a directory. Root reads past a file's$
# permissions [I], so a directory, an I/O error or an NFS root$
# squash is what is left of "unreadable"$
# (menu/logs_unreadable.golden, not as root).$
$
# Logs #########################################################$
$
# File ---------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Path                 /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  Can't read it: is a directory$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Refresh              Read the log again$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Logs #########################################################$
$
# File ---------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Path                 /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  Can't read it: is a directory$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Refresh              Read the log again$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: q$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

